<title>KUWAIT: Hyundai signs $160 mln Kuwait tanker deal.</title>
<headline>Hyundai signs $160 mln Kuwait tanker deal.</headline>
<dateline>KUWAIT 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Hyundai Heavy Industries Co on Tuesday signed a contract with the Kuwait Oil Tanker Company (KOTC) to build two 309,000-tonne oil tankers at more than $160 million, KOTC chairman said.</p>
<p>&quot;The price is over $80 million for each of the tankers,&quot; KOTC chairman Abdullah al-Roumi told reporters at the signing ceremony in Kuwait.</p>
</text>
